Ported (from core/meetings/modules in the Vexa repository):
  join/src/googlemeet/selectors.ts, admission.ts, refusal.ts, join.ts
      lobby selectors, waiting / denied / refused / expired page texts, join-button lookup
  gmeet-capture/src/gmeet-chat.ts      chat panel toggle, message list, sender and composer lookup
  gmeet-capture/src/gmeet-speakers.ts  participant tile, name and speaking-class reading
  gmeet-capture/src/pcm-capture.ts     AudioWorklet 16 kHz PCM capture
  mixed-capture-core/src/webrtc-audio-hook.ts  RTCPeerConnection remote-audio hook

Changed: rewritten in plain JavaScript as one thin script, driven from Rust; selectors and page
strings moved into one JSON file; PCM frames go to a local WebSocket as 100 ms binary frames.

Not ported on purpose: Vexa's humanized pointer input and its flag that hides browser automation.
The driver uses plain CDP input in a plain Chromium and does not hide that it is automated.
